                <pb facs="0111" n="13" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg13"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C114/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-29T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 29, 1920—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>404. Your 88, May 26, 1 p.m.</p>
                <p>Mr. Root comes to The Hague primarily as a member of the Permanent Court of The
                    Hague to pass upon the Portuguese arbitration regarding church property. As you
                    know, he is also a member of the League of Nations Organizing Committee for the
                    Permanent Court of International Justice.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
